code: kill_not_in disables notify so /tree rollback stays silent

The lineage-switch reconcile in lofi-ui calls JobRegistry::kill_not_in to
drop off-lineage jobs. The kill flipped state to Cancelled, and the driver
poll loop saw the terminal state with notify.enabled still true, so it
pushed a "job <id> cancelled: <cmd> — log: ..." notice. The UI then
delivered that to the agent as a queued user-role Notice.

That is wrong: the user just rolled back in /tree, explicitly dropping
the lineage that owned the job. Nothing about the subsidiary process
should reach the agent. The UI toast ("killed N off-lineage job(s):")
is the right channel for the user; the agent never gets a Notice.

Disable notify on the handle before kill() flips the state, so the
driver's terminal branch sees enabled=false and skips format_notice.
The restore path through jobKill, /tree's mid-run kill, and live poll
are unaffected — they still get the normal notice.